WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.523
The 2026 Digital Omnibus: what moved and what did not.

2
00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:22.723
In 2026 the EU amended the Act through the Digital Omnibus on AI, Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, published in the Official Journal in July and in force from 27 July 2026.

3
00:00:23.003 --> 00:00:43.653
The changes that matter for planning: High-risk obligations were deferred: to 2 December 2027 for standalone systems in the Annex III areas (employment, credit, and so on) and to 2 August 2028 for AI embedded in products covered by existing EU product law (Annex I).

4
00:00:43.933 --> 00:00:59.805
Generative-content marking got a transition: generative AI systems placed on the market before 2 August 2026 have until 2 December 2026 to meet the machine-readable marking duty in Article 50(2).

5
00:01:00.085 --> 00:01:12.224
AI literacy was reworded: Article 4 now requires providers and deployers to take measures to support AI literacy among their staff, without prescribing a level for any individual.

6
00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:23.384
The AI Office’s role grew: it gained exclusive competence over AI systems built on a GPAI model by the same provider, with new supervisory and fining powers.

7
00:01:23.664 --> 00:01:26.629
The GPAI chapter’s obligations did not move.

8
00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:34.163
Commentary on the Omnibus disagrees on some details, especially exactly how far transparency duties shifted.

9
00:01:34.443 --> 00:01:40.992
When a date matters for your launch, read the consolidated text on EUR-Lex rather than a summary, including this one.
